      "answer_text": "**Package to use:** `hermes-plugins/hermes-all-three` (module `hermes_all_three`). Its README says `select_context` runs a pipeline of D, then B, then A (project, then inject the catalog and fold, then rewrite oversized results).\n\n**What stops three separate plugins from being active at once:** Hermes allows only one context engine. `CONTRACT.md` (section 3, \"Single-select is a hard constraint\") says:\n- `PluginRegistration.register_context_engine` (`hermes_cli/plugins.py:717`) refuses a second engine. It checks `if self._manager._context_engine is not None`, logs a warning and returns.\n- Selection is a single `context.engine: <name>` entry in `config.yaml`, so you can only name one engine anyway.\n\nRunning all three practices therefore means one composed engine, not three co-active plugins."
    },
