      "answer_text": "**Interval:** 120,000 ms (120 s). It is `HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS = 120_000` at `.opencode/plugins/context-engineering.ts:138`. The `setInterval` at lines 185-188 sends `{ type: \"heartbeat\", session_id: id }` to the bridge for every session the plugin has seen.\n\n**Why it is needed:**\n- The bridge keeps a memory-only retention lease for each session. Large tool results are stored behind a reference, and the lease keeps those references readable.\n- Every request for a session renews its lease. During a long quiet period, such as the user thinking or an idle session, nothing renews it.\n- Without any sign of life the lease lapses after 300 s, and the reference expires after another 300 s (`.opencode/README.md:107-109`).\n- The heartbeat is a keep-alive so a reference can still be read back many turns later, after a long silence. The plugin header (lines 24-25) says the same.\n- 120 s is well inside the 300 s lease window, so one missed beat won't lose the lease. A test in `context-engineering.test.ts:281` asserts this.\n- The interval is `unref`'d (line 188), so it won't keep the process alive."
    },
